<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96240" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στᾰμίν</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στᾰμίς</span></b> , ὁ, nom. pl. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταμίνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					1.92
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; acc. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταμῖνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Moschio
				</span></i>
			 (v. infr.); 
				Ep.
			 dat. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στᾰμῐνεσσι</span>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵστημι</span>):—in pl., <i>the
			ribs</i> or <i>frame-timbers</i> of a ship, <i>which stand
			up</i> from the keel (expld. as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθὰ ξύλα,
				οἷον στήμοσιν ἐοικότα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				724.56
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.252
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
			</span></i> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				40.446
			</span></i>: but 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπηγενίδες</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Moschio
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				5.206f
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				207b
			</span></i>.</div>
